    "body": "## Overview\n\nPreserve whole-shape tuples when decomposing `Tensor.size()` nodes across compilation graph partitions, including keyword arguments.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Fixes `torch.reshape(x, shape)` becoming an invalid flattened call after splitting.\n- Rewrites keyword and nested argument references so the original size node can be removed safely. The existing `getitem` scalar path is unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\nExtended the existing graph-partition tests with positional and keyword reshape cases captured by real TorchDynamo, split around sigmoid, at batch sizes 4 and 8:\n\n```sh\nuv run --no-project --python .venv/bin/python python -m pytest \\\n  tests/compile/test_graph_partition.py -k decompose_size -q\n```\n\n| Check | Baseline | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Project size-decomposition selection | 2 passed, 2 failed | 4 passed |\n| Additional actual `VllmBackend` / standalone Inductor checks | 4 failed | 4 passed |\n| Separate default-cache, mega-AOT checks | 2 failed | 2 passed |\n| B300 one-layer dummy Llama, MRV2 + Inductor, CUDA graphs disabled | Generates `[30, 30]` | Generates `[30, 30]` |\n\nThe native environment uses Python 3.12 / Torch 2.14.0+cu130 / private vLLM ff01a6b14 runtime, with the affected baseline `backends.py` verified byte-identical to this PR's base and inspected main fb61ac07. This is not a claim of a complete latest-main runtime, official-weight model accuracy, warm-cache reload or performance improvement. The dummy-model check is non-regression coverage, not the bug reproducer; the Dynamo tests reproduce the bug.\n\nRuff check/format, whitespace checks and the project's test-tethering, SPDX, forbidden-import, new-CUDA-call and boolean-context checks pass. Full pre-commit was stopped during tool bootstrap and is not claimed passed; full CI/mypy remain unverified.\n\n## Details\n\nThe previous code expanded the size dimensions into a user's top-level positional arguments and ignored kwargs. Use the existing `fx.map_arg` traversal over both argument trees, replacing the size node with one tuple of scalar dimensions. Default lambda arguments bind the current loop node and dimensions.\n\nFound during source auditing. Open-PR searches for `_decompose_size_nodes`, size tuples and shape kwargs found no matching fix; no public issue ownership is claimed. AI assistance was used, and the human submitter reviewed every changed line.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
